TODO -- ixemul utils
====================

Medium priority
---------------

* ixstack.c

  Include a stack marker beginning exactly 12 bytes before the end of a
  file by changing the scan boundary from `i < len - 12` to
  `i <= len - 12`.

  Check the results of lseek() and the four-byte write used to update
  the requested stack size, and report seek errors, short writes and
  write errors.

* ixrun.c

  Return zero explicitly when the verbose/debug path prints the generated
  command without calling Execute().

Verification
------------

* Build all utilities with GCC 2.95.3 using the normal ixemul m68k build
  options, while retaining C89-compatible declaration placement.

* Run ixtrace with the last valid syscall number, exactly one past the
  table, and with trace lines that exactly fill or exceed the output
  buffer.

* Test localtime(), localtime_r(), gmtime_r(), ctime_r() and mktime()
  with representative valid TZif files and leap-second values.

* Test ixstack with markers at the beginning, middle and final valid
  offset of a file, and verify error handling on read-only files.

* Test ixrun with /volume/path input in both execute and verbose modes.
